        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "MOVEHOME ESTATE AGENTS... are honoured to present an outstanding three-bedroom terraced home to the open market spanning approx. 75 sq mtrs. 65 Walsh Road is an expansive, light-filled dream home that would be ideal for the professional family wishing to find a wonderful property located in the heart of Drumcondra, with every amenity on your doorstep. The property has been refurbished with great flair, impeccable taste and meticulous attention to detail, creating a stylish, low-maintenance home in a central location and truly in walk-in condition throughout.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation on the ground floor briefly comprises of a welcoming hall, front living room and open plan kitchen/dining area with a bathroom and utilty discreetly located off this area. Upstairs consists of three bedrooms and one master en-suite. To the front of the property, there is off-street parking and to the rear a beautifully landscaped garden features a decking area and a outdoor work space with convenient laneway access. The rear garden is a particular highlight, offering a private and tranquil outdoor space that creates a seamless connection between the house and the garden, making it ideal for both relaxation and entertaining. The shed to the rear could be used as a home office/study or playroom.  The roofing of the structure was designed to complement the garden and provide it's own growing area for an additional selection of plants and shrubs. The arrival of this property to the market represents a rare opportunity to purchase a bright and modern three-bedroom terraced home in this well-established Dublin neighbourhood. \r\n\r\n65 Walsh Road is located within walking distance of the city centre and convenient to the numerous shops, cafes, bars and restaurants Drumcondra village has to offer. The network of streets is known as the ‘Triangle’, and is one of the best kept secrets in Dublin. Approach the area from tree-lined Home Farm Road and you will descend a hill with a view across to the Dublin Mountains above the trees in the park below. The green open spaces nearby, including Griffith Park a mere minute away and the Botanic Garden just a stone’s throw further, and the close proximity to the city give this location the perfect combination of leafy neighbourhood life and urban buzz. Local national schools include Corpus Christi National School, Scoil Mobhi, St Patrick’s National School and Grace Park Educate Together. Secondary schools within walking distance include Scoil Caitriona, Holy Faith Secondary Schools, Dominican College, Rosmini and Clonturk. There’s also a variety of local sports clubs including Na Fíanna GAA Club and Tolka Park Shelbourne FC. For lazy weekend brunches, lunch and dinner spots like Anderson’s Café and Shouk Restaurant are only a short stroll away. For those travelling further afield, the M50, the M1 and Dublin Airport are also within easy access.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is essential to appreciate all that this wonderful home has to offer. Viewing by appointment with MOVEHOME ESTATE AGENTS ... 01-8844690"
